menu "DataDrive encryption"

    config PD_CRYPT_SELFTEST
        bool "AES-256-XTS self-test at boot (IEEE P1619 vectors)"
        default y
        help
            Checks both AES-XTS implementations against known answers (and against each other
            across 20 sectors) before the drive can be unlocked or set up, and logs the crypto
            throughput. Takes a few milliseconds. If the direct hardware path fails, mbedtls is
            used; if both fail, encryption is refused. Off: only one known-answer test of the
            path in use (always run).

    config PD_CRYPT_HW_DIRECT
        bool "Drive the AES peripheral directly (fast path)"
        default y
        help
            mbedtls' XTS starts one DMA transfer per 16-byte block (33 per sector). The direct
            path uses the AES peripheral in register mode under the same hardware lock and loads
            each key once per 16 sectors. Off: mbedtls only.

    config PD_CRYPT_SCRATCH_KB
        int "Encryption write buffer (KiB, allocated only while unlocked)"
        default 8
        range 1 32
        help
            Writes are encrypted into this buffer (never in the caller's buffer). 8 KiB matches
            the USB MSC transfer size; larger values mean fewer, longer SD card writes for
            uploads at the cost of heap.

    config PD_CRYPT_KDF_TARGET_MS
        int "Target time of the password key derivation (ms)"
        default 2000
        range 500 5000
        help
            PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 iterations are calibrated at setup / password change so that one
            derivation takes about this long on the device (fastest of 5 probes; never less
            than half a second's worth). Unlocking takes about this long, too.

    config PD_CRYPT_OVERWRITE_MAX_MB
        int "Overwrite fallback limit when the medium cannot be erased (MB)"
        default 64
        range 0 100000
        help
            Setup erases the whole medium (SD ERASE command, flash erase). If a card refuses
            ERASE, the affected sectors are overwritten with zeros instead, up to this amount;
            beyond it setup is refused, because overwriting a large card takes hours.

endmenu
